<article class="env-lemma" id="045Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/045Y">Lemma <span data-tag="045Y">39.20.4</span>.</a> Let $\tau \in \{ Zariski, {\acute{e}tale}, fppf, smooth, syntomic\} $. Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $j : R \to U \times _ S U$ be a pre-equivalence relation over $S$. Assume $U, R, S$ are objects of a $\tau $-site $\mathit{Sch}_\tau $. For $T \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits ((\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau )$ and $a, b \in U(T)$ the following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$a$ and $b$ map to the same element of $(U/R)(T)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a $\tau $-covering $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} $ of $T$ and morphisms $r_ i : T_ i \to R$ such that $a \circ f_ i = s \circ r_ i$ and $b \circ f_ i = t \circ r_ i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In other words, in this case the map of $\tau $-sheaves </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  h_ R \longrightarrow h_ U \times _{U/R} h_ U  \]
</div>
  <p> is surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: The reason this works is that the presheaf (<a href="/tag/02VF" data-tag="02VF">39.20.0.1</a>) in this case is really given by $T \mapsto U(T)/j(R(T))$ as $j(R(T)) \subset U(T) \times U(T)$ is an equivalence relation, see Definition <a href="/tag/022P" data-tag="022P">39.3.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>